 The company sells its insurance products in all 50 states, the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, and the U.S. Virgin Islands primarily through a network of independent insurance brokers. Kinsale Capital Group, Inc. was founded in 2009 and is headquartered in Richmond, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Patrick Kehoe J.D. | Chairman of the Board, CEO & President | Age 59 | Compensation: $4.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 711 people. Revenue per employee of $2.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 33%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $1.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $25K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Kinsale Capital Group, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $8.6B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +32% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $990M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 53 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -8.9% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 61\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[